{"answer":"None of the supplied papers discuss graph-structured rerankers or any mechanism for preventing repetitive item lists in generative reranking.

The closest topic is self-referential/behavioral structures in LLMs: several papers study how specific internal mechanisms or prompting conditions shape structured outputs and self-reports, including mechanistic gating of first-person experience claims ([4]) and conditions for behavioral self-awareness that can be induced and localized ([10]). However, these abstracts do not connect to graph structure or to repetition reduction in reranking item lists.

Therefore, the results here do not answer how graph structure can stop generative rerankers from producing repetitive item lists.","grounded":false}
